  {
   "id": "short_vowels",
   "afterGroup": 1,
   "title": "Short vowels",
   "intro": [
    "Arabic letters are consonants. Small marks above or below a letter tell you the short vowel that follows it.",
    "A slanted line above the letter is fatha (a). A slanted line below is kasra (i). A small curl above is damma (u).",
    "The letter alif after a fatha makes the vowel long: bā."
   ],
   "reminder": "Fatha is a line above (a), kasra a line below (i), damma a small curl above (u).",
   "marks": [
    "fatha",
    "kasra",
    "damma"
   ],
   "introduces": [],
