   "id": "tanwin",
   "afterGroup": 5,
   "title": "Tanwin: the -n ending",
   "intro": [
    "Doubled vowel marks at the end of a word are tanwin. They add an n sound: -an, -un or -in.",
    "They mark a noun as indefinite, like \"a door\". Fathatan is usually written with an alif after it."
   ],
   "reminder": "Two marks on the last letter add -n: fatha pair is -an, damma pair is -un, kasra pair is -in.",
   "marks": [
    "fathatan",
    "dammatan",
    "kasratan"
   ],
